@startuml
title 3. Take Cards (Socket)

legend top
This diagram represents the action of taking cards from the board.
The client sends a TakeCardsRequest specifying the chosen cards from the upper and lower rows.
The Controller delegates the request to the InGamePhase, which invokes the Game model.
The model validates the move, including card selection consistency and resource costs.
If successful, the updated game state is returned; otherwise, an error message is sent.
endlegend

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #2F4F4F
    LifeLineBorderColor #708090
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
    ParticipantBorderColor #5F6F7F
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAEFF7
    ActorBorderColor #5F6F7F
    ActorBackgroundColor #EAEFF7
    GroupBorderColor #444444
    GroupBackgroundColor #FDFDFD
    BoxBorderColor #7F8C8D
    BoxBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
}

actor Player

box "Client Node" #DDF3F4
participant View
participant VirtualSocketServer
end box

box "Server Node" #F7F5D6
participant "SocketClientHandler\n(VirtualView)" as Handler
participant Controller
participant InGamePhase
participant "Game\n(Model)" as Game
end box

Player -> View : selectCards(upper, lower)
View -> VirtualSocketServer : takeCards(nickname, upper, lower)
VirtualSocketServer -> Handler : TakeCardsRequest(nickname, upper, lower)

note right of Handler
The request contains the cards\nselected from the upper and lower rows.
end note

Handler -> Controller : takeCards(nickname, upper, lower)
Controller -> InGamePhase : handleTakeCards(this, nickname, upper, lower)
InGamePhase -> Game : takeCards(player, upper, lower)

alt [Valid move]
    Game --> InGamePhase : return
    InGamePhase --> Controller : success
    Controller -> Handler : GameUpdated(gameState)
    Handler -> VirtualSocketServer : GameUpdated(gameState)
    VirtualSocketServer -> View : updateBoard(gameState)
else [Insufficient food]
    Game --> InGamePhase : throw InsufficientFoodException
    InGamePhase --> Controller : propagate exception
    Controller -> Handler : Error("Not enough food")
    Handler -> VirtualSocketServer : Error("Not enough food")
    VirtualSocketServer -> View : showError("Not enough food")
else [Invalid card selection]
    Game --> InGamePhase : throw InvalidMoveException
    InGamePhase --> Controller : propagate exception
    Controller -> Handler : Error("Invalid card selection")
    Handler -> VirtualSocketServer : Error("Invalid card selection")
    VirtualSocketServer -> View : showError("Invalid card selection")
end

note right of Game
The model validates:
- current phase
- active player
- selected cards consistency
- food cost, if buildings are chosen
Then it updates the player's state and the board.
end note

@enduml